      <marc:subfield code="a">A living word-spirit, vibrant for a thousand years, born into the household of emperors. How fortunate he was—yet how tragically doomed! In this powerful new work, author Tsai Shih-Ping delves into the creative life and fatal destiny of Li Houzhu of the Southern Tang. Through the ages, countless masters of Chinese lyric poetry have emerged—so why does Li Houzhu hold an irreplaceable place among them?</marc:subfield>
